messages:
Ashley: Quick review request — about to merge a small terraform PR that wires KMS grants + IRSA for model-server in staging. Can someone do a quick sanity check? PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/infra/pull/412

Snippet I'm using:
```hcl
resource "aws_iam_role" "model_server_irsa" {
  name = "model-server-irsa"
  assume_role_policy = data.aws_iam_policy_document.irsa_auth.json
}

resource "kubernetes_service_account" "model_server_sa" {
  metadata {
    name = "model-server"
    namespace = "inference"
    annotations = {
      "eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn" = aws_iam_role.model_server_irsa.arn
    }
  }
}

resource "aws_kms_key" "model_key" {
  description = "Model encryption key for staging"
}

resource "aws_kms_grant" "model_server_decrypt" {
  name = "model-server-decrypt"
  key_id = aws_kms_key.model_key.key_id
  grantee_principal = aws_iam_role.model_server_irsa.arn
  operations = ["Decrypt", "GenerateDataKey"]
}
```

Kevin: Quick skim — looks sensible. Two calls out:
- Make sure the assume_role_policy uses `sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity` and includes a StringEquals condition on `sub` matching `system:serviceaccount:inference:model-server` (exact). Also confirm the cluster OIDC issuer is set in the provider config.
- For KMS: consider adding `Encrypt` if you do envelope encryption on the node side, and include `kms:DescribeKey` in the role's inline policy so the role can query key metadata.

Sam: Add a small `depends_on = [aws_iam_role.model_server_irsa]` to the kms grant so TF doesn't race at apply time. We've hit a race where the grant was created before the role propagated to KMS, which caused a failure. Also double-check the key policy doesn't explicitly block grants from principals in the account. Minimal grant example:
```hcl
resource "aws_kms_grant" "model_server_decrypt" {
  key_id = aws_kms_key.model_key.key_id
  grantee_principal = aws_iam_role.model_server_irsa.arn
  operations = ["Decrypt", "GenerateDataKey"]
  depends_on = [aws_iam_role.model_server_irsa]
}
```

Ashley: Thanks both. I'll add the assume_role_policy tweak, include `Encrypt` for safety, and the depends_on. Pushing a small commit now.

infra-bot: Running `terraform plan` for branch iam/kms-irsa — Plan: 0 to add, 1 to change, 0 to destroy. No errors.

Kevin: LGTM after those changes. Leave a note on the PR about the OIDC issuer URL so on-call can rebind if the cluster is re-created.

Ashley: Done and pushed. @Sam can you sanity-check the live service account mapping after merge? :thumbsup:

Sam: Yep, will check once merged.

